+# Philosophy
+
+For anyone proposing a service or reviewing one. These tenets guide the trade-off between a new service's benefits
+and the work volunteers take on to operate it. In [issue 70](../notes/issue-70.md), a proposal to add Elasticsearch
+reopened the "one more service" argument for the third time that year; the team asked for the rule to be written
+down so the next proposal starts from it.
+
+## Tenets
+
+### Add a service we operate only when Postgres cannot meet the need and two volunteers can restore it.
+
+This rules out adding a service just because it is a familiar tool for the job, or because one volunteer can set it
+up: a proposal must show what Postgres cannot do and who the two volunteers able to restore the service are. Both
+conditions must hold before adding to the [existing system](architecture.md).
+
+Applied in [keeping sessions in the database](adr/0001-keep-sessions-in-the-database.md) and
+[running background jobs on Postgres](adr/0002-run-background-jobs-on-postgres.md). Issue 70 applied the same rule to
+search: Postgres full-text search met the reported need, so the Elasticsearch proposal was dropped.
+
+This permits external services: the card gateway is already outside larder, and a hosted service that nobody on the
+team has to operate is acceptable. The two conditions above apply to services the volunteers would operate.
